Package: randomNames
Version: 1.7-0.0
Date: 2026-10-31
Title: Generate Random Given and Surnames
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports: cli, data.table (>= 1.14.0), stats, toOrdinal (>= 1.4-0.0), utils
Suggests: knitr, rmarkdown, testthat (>= 3.0.0), withr
Authors@R: c(
    person("Damian W.", "Betebenner", email = "dbetebenner@nciea.org", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0476-5599")),
    person("Lambert", "Joshua", role = "ctb"),
    person("Center for Assessment", role = "cph"))
Description: Generates gender and ethnicity correct first and/or last names. Names are chosen proportionally based upon their probability of appearing in a large scale data base of real names, so a roster of random names looks like a roster of real ones. Useful for anonymising results that would otherwise identify people.
URL: https://centerforassessment.github.io/randomNames/, https://github.com/CenterForAssessment/randomNames/, https://cran.r-project.org/package=randomNames
